<title>GERMANY: German cabinet approves plan to sell oil reserves.</title>
<headline>German cabinet approves plan to sell oil reserves.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl's cabinet on Friday approved a plan to sell government crude oil reserves in an effort to raise cash and reduce the deficit, a Finance Ministry spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>In 1997, the government hopes to raise 400 million marks through such sales. The first tranche, of about 2.8 million barrels of oil, is expected in a few weeks, a government source said earlier.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
